.TH CC_BINDINGS_FROM_RS 1 "" "Crubit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cc_bindings_from_rs \- generate C++ bindings for a Rust crate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cc_bindings_from_rs
.BI \-\-h\-out " FILE"
.BI \-\-rs\-out " FILE"
.BI \-\-crubit\-support\-path\-format " STRING"
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.B \-\-
.RI [ RUSTC_ARG ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cc_bindings_from_rs
is part of Crubit, a set of tools for C++ and Rust interoperability. It reads a
Rust crate and writes a C++ header plus a Rust source file that together let C++
call into that crate without hand-written FFI glue.
.PP
The tool drives the Rust compiler through its internal APIs, so it must be built
by, and run against, the same
.B rustc
that compiles the crate it generates bindings for. Bindings generated by one
rustc version are not guaranteed to work with another.
.PP
Trailing arguments after a literal
.B \-\-
are passed through to the Rust compiler. They describe the crate to read, in the
same form
.BR rustc (1)
takes.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Required"
.TP
.BI \-\-h\-out " FILE"
Write the generated C++ header to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI \-\-rs\-out " FILE"
Write the generated Rust implementation to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI \-\-crubit\-support\-path\-format " STRING"
How to
.B #include
the Crubit C++ support library headers, with
.B {header}
as the placeholder. For example
.B <crubit/support/{header}>
produces
.BR "#include <crubit/support/hdr.h>" .
.SS "Output"
.TP
.BI \-\-h\-out\-include\-guard " STRING"
Use
.I STRING
as the include guard of the generated C++ header.
.TP
.BI \-\-crubit\-debug\-path\-format " STRING"
Format for path cross-references in the generated \*(lqGenerated from\*(rq
comments, so that a code navigation system can turn them into links. The
placeholders are
.B {path}
for the original Rust source file and
.B {line}
for the line number in it. Only real files on disk use this format; virtual
files have a hardcoded one.
.TP
.BI \-\-error\-report\-out " FILE"
Write an error report to
.IR FILE .
.SS "Formatting"
.TP
.BI \-\-clang\-format\-exe\-path " FILE"
Run
.I FILE
to format the generated C++ header. Generated code is left unformatted if this
is omitted.
.TP
.BI \-\-rustfmt\-exe\-path " FILE"
Run
.I FILE
to format the generated Rust source. Generated code is left unformatted if this
is omitted.
.TP
.BI \-\-rustfmt\-config\-path " FILE"
Use
.I FILE
instead of the default rustfmt configuration. Only honoured together with
.BR \-\-rustfmt\-exe\-path .
.SS "Dependency crates"
.TP
.BI \-\-crate\-header " CRATE_NAME=INCLUDE_PATH"
Give the include path of bindings for a dependency crate, as generated by an
earlier run of Crubit. May be repeated. A crate name is not guaranteed to be
globally unique across versions and compilation flags.
.TP
.BI \-\-crate\-namespace " CRATE_NAME=NAMESPACE"
Set the top-level C++ namespace of the bindings for
.IR CRATE_NAME .
May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-crate\-rename " CRATE_NAME=RENAMED"
Use
.I RENAMED
in place of
.I CRATE_NAME
inside the generated bindings. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-extern " CRATE_NAME=FILE"
Declare an explicit dependency of binding generation. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-L " [\fIKIND\fP=]PATH"
Add
.I PATH
to the directories searched for dependencies. Passed through to the Rust
compiler, which parses any
.I KIND
prefix. May be repeated.
.SS "Crubit features"
.TP
.BI \-\-default\-features " CRUBIT_FEATURES"
Comma-separated Crubit feature flags enabled for all crates. Empty by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-crate\-feature " CRATE_NAME=CRUBIT_FEATURE"
Enable
.I CRUBIT_FEATURE
for
.IR CRATE_NAME .
May be repeated. The crate name
.B self
refers to the crate whose bindings are being generated. Every crate must have
its features fully specified, and consistently across rustc invocations, or the
behaviour is undefined.
.TP
.BI \-\-crate\-disabled\-feature " CRATE_NAME=CRUBIT_FEATURE"
Disable
.I CRUBIT_FEATURE
for
.IR CRATE_NAME .
May be repeated. A feature named here wins over
.B \-\-default\-features
and
.BR \-\-crate\-feature .
.SS "Compilation"
.TP
.BI \-\-source\-crate\-name " STRING"
Name of the crate to generate bindings for. If given, it must match an extern
crate provided in the trailing rustc arguments. If omitted, bindings are
generated for the crate being compiled by those arguments.
.TP
.BI \-\-target " STRING"
Target triple of the compilation. Must match the triple the Rust crate being
bound was originally compiled with.
.TP
.BI \-\-sysroot " STRING"
Sysroot of the compilation.
.TP
.BI \-\-enable\-rmeta\-interface " BOOL"
Use the newer interface that generates bindings from
.B .rmeta
files. Defaults to
.BR true .
.TP
.BI \-\-ignore\-symbols\-from\-files " FILE"
Exclude symbols defined in
.I FILE
from the generated bindings. May be repeated.
.SS "Kythe"
.TP
.BI \-\-kythe\-annotations " BOOL"
Emit extra source information for cross-references. Defaults to
.BR false .
.TP
.BI \-\-kythe\-default\-corpus " STRING"
Default corpus for Kythe vnames. Defaults to
.BR corpus .
.SS "Other"
.TP
.BI \-\-is\-golden\-test " BOOL"
Omit unnecessary information such as source locations, to reduce noise in golden
tests, and stop mangling thunk names. Using this in production may cause
undefined behaviour. Defaults to
.BR false .
.TP
.BI \-\-extra\-rs\-srcs\-include " FILE"
Add a header to
.B #include
and re-export via IWYU in the generated C++ header, so that C++ callers receive
the includes needed by embedded C++ declarations such as
.BR inline_cpp! .
May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-portable\-abi\-compatible " BOOL"
Use the stricter definition of ABI compatibility. Defaults to
.BR false .
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.SH ARGUMENT FILES
Any argument of the form
.BI @ FILE
is expanded before parsing, with one argument per line of
.IR FILE .
Expansion applies to Crubit's own options as well as to the trailing rustc
arguments.
.SH EXAMPLE
Generate bindings for a crate named
.BR example ,
whose
.B .rmeta
was produced by the same rustc:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cc_bindings_from_rs \\
    \-\-h\-out=example_cc_api.h \\
    \-\-rs\-out=example_cc_api_impl.rs \\
    \-\-crubit\-support\-path\-format=<crubit/support/{header}> \\
    \-\- \\
    \-\-crate\-type=lib \\
    \-\-crate\-name=example \\
    \-L dependency=/path/to/deps
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success. Non-zero if argument parsing fails or if binding generation
reports an error.
.SH NOTES
The generated code includes headers from the Crubit C++ support library under
.IR support/ .
Pass
.B \-\-crubit\-support\-path\-format
to say how those headers are reached in your build, for example
.B <crubit/support/{header}>
or
.BR \(dqthird_party/crubit/support/{header}\(dq .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rustc (1),
.BR cargo (1)
.PP
The Crubit documentation, in
.I docs/
and rendered at
.IR https://github.com/google/crubit .
